 equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=x\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a function and the known \nsolutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the quotients of the known solutions.\n\n- The function $y(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡x)$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79826" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "001e6c31292f1d3e7a2fe034dcf5f0bb4dc83c5860127b741446ebb7c34d7d54"} {"question" "q-79826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79826" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={x}^{2}$ is a solution to the equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-4y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\n- $y(x)=3{x}^{4}$\n- $y(x)=-{x}^{2}$\n- $y(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "According to the superposition principle, if the function ${y}_{1}(x)$ is a solution to a homogeneous, linear differential equation, and $c$ is a constant, then $y(x)=c{y}_{1}(x)$ is also a solution to the equation.\n\nLet's consider each option:\n\n- The function $y(x)=3{x}^{4}$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle because $y(x)={x}^{4}$ is not a solution.\n\n- The function $y(x)=-{x}^{2}$ is a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. In this case, $c=-1.$\n\n- The function $y(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x$ is **not** guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79830" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "001e6c31292f1d3e7a2fe034dcf5f0bb4dc83c5860127b741446ebb7c34d7d54"} {"question" "q-79830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II and III"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79830" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-131022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)={x}^{4}$ is a solution to the equation ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-7x{y}^{′}+16y=0,$ then according to the superposition principle which of the following must also be a solution to the equation?\n\n- $y(x)=-2{x}^{4}$\n- $y(x)={x}^{4}\\sqrt{x}$\n- $y(x)=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{{e}^{x}}$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/ques