 guaranteed to be a solution of the equation by the superposition principle. The superposition principle does not extend to the product of a non-constant function and a known solution.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-131020" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "001e6c31292f1d3e7a2fe034dcf5f0bb4dc83c5860127b741446ebb7c34d7d54"} {"question" "q-131020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-131020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "I, II, and III"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-131020" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "I and II only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14085055/state.json" "file_sha256" "ee806d7632c7d246672232e2eee8608ec43343e0c39d611d09ae3e2af8801721"} {"question" "q-79730" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${y}_{1}(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)$ is a solution to a ho